1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunigunde_of_Sternberg wikipedia] - '''Kunigunde of Sternberg''' (Czech: Kunhuta ze Šternberka; 18 November 1425, Konopiště – 19 November 1449, Poděbrady) was the first wife of '''Geor
2 CONC ge of Poděbrady''', who later became King of Bohemia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Kunigunde'''s parents were the Bohemian nobles '''Smil of Sternberg''' († 1431) and '''Barbara of Pardubice''' († 1433). In 1441 she married then 21-year-old '''George of Poděbrady''', who had been captain of the old Bohemian c
2 CONC ircle of Stará Boleslav[1] since 1440. This marriage produced three sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Boček (1442–1496), Victor, (1443–1500) and 'Henry the Elder (1448–1498)
2 CONT
2 CONT and three daughters: Barbara (1446–1474), married first with '''Henry of Lipé''' (Jindřich z Lipé, † 1469), and second with '''Jan Křinecký''' of Ronov, Catherine (1449–1464) and Zdenka (1449–1510)
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1444 '''Kunigunde''' founded a hospital in Poděbrady. It was named after her and remained in operation until the beginning of the 20th Century. She also established a foundation for youth education, school construction and reha
2 CONC bilitation of prisoners.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1449, the day after her twenty-fourth birthday and several days after giving birth to twin daughters, and was buried in the parish church Exaltation of the Holy Cross in Poděbrady.
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnotes 1. Adolf Bachmann (1878) (in German). "George of Poděbrady". In Allgemeine Deutsche Biographie (ADB). 8. Leipzig: Duncker & Humblot. pp. 602–610
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunigunde_von_Sternberg
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cun%C3%A9gonde_de_Sternberg
