1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_of_Hesse
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT Philip I, Landgrave of Hesse
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip married in Dresden on 11 December 1523 Christine of Saxony (daughter of George, Duke of Saxony) and had in this marriage 10 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes (31 May 1527 – 4 November 1555), married:
2 CONT
2 CONT in Marburg on 9 January 1541 to Elector Maurice of Saxony;
2 CONT
2 CONT in Weimar on 26 May 1555 to Duke John Frederick II, Duke of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice, Elector of Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT After Maurice came of age, in 1539, his parents began to look for a wife for him. The favorite was Philip's eldest daughter, Agnes. The marriage plans threatened to fail, however, because the illegal double marriage of the Landgra
2 CONC ve. Without the knowledge of his parents, Maurice remained committed to his engagement with Agnes. The wedding, particularly disapproved by his mother, took place in Marburg on 9 January 1541. Letters from that time illustrate the
2 CONC  strong mutual devotion of the couple. Together they had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna (b. Dresden, 23 December 1544 – d. Dresden, 18 December 1577), married on 24 August 1561 to Prince William I of Orange-Nassau. They divorced in 1574.
2 CONT
2 CONT Albrecht (b. Dresden, 28 November 1545 – d. Dresden, 12 April 1546).
