1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elisabeth of Hesse (13 February 1539 – 14 March 1582) was a German noblewoman. She was a daughter of Philip I, Landgrave of Hesse and Christine of Saxony, daughter of George, Duke of Saxony.  On 8 July 1560 she mar
2 CONC ried Louis VI, Elector Palatine. They had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Marie (1561–1589), married Charles IX of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (15 June – 2 November 1562)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothea Elisabeth (12 January – 7 March 1565)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothea (1566–1567)
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Philip (19 October 1567 – 14 November 1568)
2 CONT
2 CONT Johann Friedrich (died within a month of birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwig (died within three months of birth)
2 CONT
2 CONT Katharina (1572–1586)
2 CONT
2 CONT Christine (1573–1619)
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick (1574–1610), succeeded as Elector Palatine
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip (4 May 1575 – 9 August 1575)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth (1576–1577)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth was a niece of Elizabeth of Rochlitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links:==
2 CONT
