2 CONT
2 CONT Heer van Beverweerd]. Retrieved 7 October 2009.
2 CONT
2 CONT References: See: Reinildis van Ditzhuyzen, Oranje-Nassau: Een biografisch woordenboek, Haarlem 2004, 171-173 (with a portrait, ca. 1650)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_of_Nassau-Beverweerd
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis of Nassau, Lord of De Lek and Beverweerd (1602 – 28 February 1665) was a Dutch soldier. He was the illegitimate son of Margaretha van Mechelen and Maurice of Nassau, Prince of Orange, and so a collateral member of the House 
2 CONC of Orange-Nassau. He was a Lord of the heerlijkheid De Lek and Beverweerd. From his father he inherited the estate of Beverweerd; and when his older brother Willem died in 1627 he inherited his estate as well.
