2 CONT '''WILLEM "Taciturnus/the Silent" Graf von Nassau, Katzenelnbogen, Vianden und Diez, son of WILHELM I "der Reiche" Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg in Dillenburg, Siegen, Vianden und [halb] Diez & his second wife Juliane von Stolberg-We
2 CONC rnigerode (Dillenburg 24 Apr 1533-murdered Delft 10 Jul 1584, bur Delft Nieuwe Kerk).'''  He succeeded in 1544 as Prince d'Orange.  Heer van Breda, Lek, Steenbergen, Sichem, Diest, Herstal, Grimbergen, Rumpst, Zundert, Gageldonck 
2 CONC and Assche, Burggraf van Antwerpen.  Heer van Vere en Vlissingen.  Stadhouder of Holland, Seeland and Utrecht.  WILLEM I  Stadhouder of the Netherlands 1581. '''m firstly (Büren 8 Jul 1551) ANNA van Egmond Gravin van Büren, Leerda
2 CONC m en Lingen, Vrouwe van Ijsselstein, Grave, Sint-Maartensdijk, Cortgene en Cranendonck, daughter of MAXIMILIAAN Graaf van Buren Stadhouder of Friesland & his wife Françoise Dame de Lannoy (Grave Mar 1533-Breda 24 Mar 1558, bur Bre
2 CONC da). m secondly (Leipzig 24 Aug 1561, divorced 1574) ANNA von Sachsen, daughter of MORITZ Elector of Saxony & his wife Agnes von Hessen (Dresden 23 Dec 1544-Dresden 18 Dec 1577, bur Freiberg Cathedral). m thirdly (Den Briel 12 Jul
2 CONC  1574) CHARLOTTE de Bourbon, daughter of LOUIS de Bourbon Duc de Montpensier & his first wife Jacqueline de Longwy Ctss de Bar-sur-Seine (-Antwerp 6 May 1582, bur Antwerp, church of Notre-Dame).  Nun 1559.  Abbess of Jouarre 1571.
2 CONC   She renounced her vows in 1572 when she went to the court of Friedrich III Elector Palatine and converted to Calvinism.   m fourthly (Antwerp 24 Apr 1583) as her second husband, LOUISE de Coligny, widow of CHARLES Seigneur de Th
2 CONC éligny en Rouergue, daughter of GASPARD [II] Comte de Coligny, Seigneur de Châtillon-sur-Loing [Amiral de France] & his wife Charlotte de Laval (Châtillon-sur-Loing 28 Sep 1555-Fontainebleau 13 Nov 1620, bur Delft Nieuwe Kerk). ''
2 CONC ''''Mistress (1):  EVA Elinx, daughter of ---.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Willem I & his first wife had three children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1.         ['''MARIA'''] 22 Nov 1553-after 22 Jul 1555).  
2 CONT * 2.         '''FILIPS WILLEM''' (Buren 19 Dec 1554-Brussels 20 Feb 1618, bur Delft). ''' He succeeded his mother in 1558 as Graaf van Buren.'''  He was imprisoned in Spain 1568-1596.  He succeeded his father in 1584 as FILIPS WIL
2 CONC LEM Prins van Oranje.  '''m contract Paris 19 Nov 1606, Château de Valléry 21 Nov 1606) ELEONORE de Bourbon, daughter of HENRI de Bourbon Prince de Condé, Duc d'Enghien & his second wife Charlotte de Trémoïlle (30 Apr 1587-Château
2 CONC  de Muret 20 Jan 1619, bur Valléry).'''  
2 CONT * 3.         '''MARIA''' (Breda 7 Feb 1556-Buren 10 Oct 1616, bur Öhringen Stiftskirche).  '''m (Buren 7 Feb 1595) PHILIPP Graf von Hohenlohe, son of --- (-Ijsselstein 6 Mar 1606, bur Öhringen Stiftskirche).'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Willem I & his second wife had five children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4.         '''daughter''' (b and d Brussels 1 Nov 1562).  
2 CONT * 5.         '''ANNA''' (5 Nov 1563-Franeker 13 Jun 1588, bur Leeuwarden).'''  m (Franeker 25 Nov 1587) WILHELM LUDWIG Graf von Nassau-Dillenburg Stadhouder of Friesland and Groningen, son of JOHANN VI "der Ältere" Graf von Nassau
2 CONC -Dillenburg in Dillenburg, Siegen, Hadamar und Diez & his first wife Elisabeth von Leuchtenberg (Siegen 13 Mar 1560-Leeuwarden 31 May 1620, bur Leeuwarden).'''  He succeeded in 1607 as WILHELM LUDWIG "Us Heit" Graf von Nassau-Dill
2 CONC enburg.  
2 CONT * 6.         '''MAURITIUS AUGUST PHILIPP''' (Brussels 18 Dec 1564-Brussels 8 Dec 1566).  
2 CONT * 7.         '''MAURITS''' (Dillenburg 13 Nov 1567-The Hague 23 Apr 1625, bur Delft).  Stadhouder and Captain-General of Holland and Seeland 1585.  Stadhouder of Utrecht, Geldern and Overijssel 1590.  Graf von Mörs 1600.  In Linge
2 CONC n und Willemstad 1609.  '''He succeeded his half-brother in 1618 as MAURITS Prins van Oranje, Baron van Breda, Graaf van Buren en Leerdam.  Stadhouder of Groningen and Drenthe 1620.'''  '''Mistress (1):  MARGARETHA van Mechelen, d
2 CONC aughter of --- ([1581]-1662).  Mistress (2):  CORNELIA Jacobsdochter, daughter of JACOB ---.  Mistress (3):  URSULA de Rijck, daughter of ---.  Mistress (4):  ANNA van der Kelder, daughter of ---.  Mistress (5):  DELIANA de Backer
2 CONC , daughter of ---.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maurits had three illegitimate children by Mistress (1), MARGARETHA van Mechelen'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''LODEWIJK van Nassau''' (1602-The Hague 1665).  Heer van Beverweerd en der Lek.  Governor of Bergen op Zoom.  '''m (1630). ISABELLA Graviin von Horne, daughter of --- (-1664).  GRAVEN van NASSAU de LEK.''' 
2 CONT * b)         '''WILLEM van Nassau''' ([1601-killed in battle 1627).  Heer van de Lek.  '''m (Sluis 1627) ANNA van der Noot Vrouwe van Hoogwoud, daughter of --- (-1642).  van NASSAU.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maurits had one illegitimate child by Mistress (2), CORNELIA Jacobsdochter'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * c)         '''ANNA''' (-1673).  '''m ([1636]) FRANÇOIS de Ferrier Seigneur de Morsant, son of --- (-1647).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maurits had two illegitimate children by Mistress (3), URSULA de Rijck''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * d)         '''ELISABETH''' (1611-, bur Breda 1679).  
2 CONT * e)         '''KAREL''' (Delft [1612]-killed in battle Ponto Calvo Brazil 1637).  '''m (1630) MARGARETA van Bodeghem, daughter of ---.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Karel & his wife had one child: ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          '''MARIA''' (1634-after 1651).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maurits had one illegitimate child by Mistress (4), ANNA van der Kelder'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * f)          '''KAREL MAURITS''' (-after 1636[1322]).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Maurits had one illegitimate child by Mistress (5), DELIANA de Backer'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * g)         '''ELEONORA (-[1693/1703]).  married (The Hague 1643) GERHARD BERNHARD Freiherr von Pölnitz, (-Berlin 1679).'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 8.         '''EMILIA Pss van Oranje-Nassau''' (Köln 10 Apr 1569-Geneva 16 Mar 1629, bur Geneva Saint-Pierre).  Dame de Frangins [Vaud] 1626.  m (The Hague 17 Nov 1597) as his first wife, dom MANOEL de Portugal, illegitimate son 
2 CONC of dom ANTONIO de Portugal & his mistress Anna Barbosa (-Brussels 22 Jun 1638, bur Brussels Franciscan Church).  Self-styled “dom MANOEL I "Prince" of Portugal”, he claimed the throne of Portugal in 1595 on the death of his father
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Willem I & his third wife had six children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 9.         '''LUISE JULIANE''' (Delft 31 Mar 1576-Königsberg in Preußen 15 Mar 1644, bur Königsberg Cathedral).  Regent of the Palatinate 1610-1611 for her son Friedrich V.  She lived at the court of her son-in-law Georg Wilhelm
2 CONC  Elector of Brandenburg, and left Berlin with them for Königsberg during the Thirty Years War. '''m (Dillenburg 23 Jun 1593) FRIEDRICH IV Elector Palatine, son of LUDWIG VI Elector Palatine & his first wife Elisabeth Landgräfin vo
2 CONC n Hessen (Amberg 5 Mar 1574-Heidelberg 9 Sep 1610, bur Heidelberg Heilige Geist). ''' 
2 CONT * 10.      '''ELISABETH''' (Middelburg 26 Mar 1577-Sedan 3 Sep 1642, bur Sedan).  m (The Hague 15 Apr 1595) as his second wife, HENRI de la Tour Duc de Bouillon, Prince de Sedan, son of FRANÇOIS [III] de la Tour Vicomte de Turenne
2 CONC  & his wife Eléonore de Montmorency (Joze en Auvergne 28 Sep 1555-Sedan 25 Mar 1623, bur Sedan).  
2 CONT * 11.      '''KATHARINA BELGICA''' (Antwerp 3 Jul 1578-The Hague 12 Apr 1648, bur Delft).  Regent 1612.  m (Dillenburg 22 Oct 1596) PHILIPP LUDWIG II Graf von Hanau-Münzenberg, son of --- (-9 Aug 1612).  
2 CONT * 12.      '''CHARLOTTE FLANDRINA''' (Antwerp 18 Aug 1579-16 Apr 1640).  Abbess of Sainte Croix near Poitiers.  
2 CONT * 13.      '''CHARLOTTE BRABANTINA''' (Antwerp 17 Sep 1580-Aug 1631).  m (Châtellerault 11 Mar 1598) CLAUDE de la Trémoïlle Duc de Thouars, son of LOUIS [III] de la Trémoïlle Duc de Thouars & his wife Jeanne de Montmorency (1566-C
2 CONC hâteau de Thouars 25 Oct 1604).  
2 CONT * 14.      '''EMILIA SECUNDA ANTWERPIANA''' (Antwerp 9 Dec 1581-Landsberg 28 Sep 1657, bur Meisenheim).  m (Zweibrücken 4 Jul 1616) FRIEDRICH KASIMIR Pfalzgraf von Zweibrücken in Landsberg, son of JOHANN Pfalzgraf von Zweibrücken 
2 CONC & his wife Magdalene Pss von Kleve (Zweibrücken 10 Jun 1585-Montfort, Côte d’Or 30 Sep 1645, bur Zweibrücken Alexanderkirche).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Willem I & his fourth wife had one child:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 15.      '''FREDERIK HENDRIK''' (Delft 1584-The Hague 1647).  He succeeded his brother 1625 as Prins van Oranje, Graf von Nassau, Katzelnbogen, Vianden, Diez, Lingen, Mörs, Buren en Leerdam, Marquis de Vere en Vlissingen, Heer e
2 CONC n Baron van Breda, Grave en Cuyck.   FREDERIK HENDRIK Stadhouder of the Netherlands.  '''m (The Hague 1625) AMALIE Gräfin zu Solms-Braunfels, daughter of --- (Braunfels 31 Aug 1602-The Hague 8 Sep 1675).  Mistress (1):  MARGARETA 
2 CONC KATHARINA Bruyne, daughter of ---. ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Frederik Hendrik & his wife had nine children: ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * a)         '''WILLEM''' (The Hague 27 May 1626-Binnenhof Palace, The Hague 27 Oct/6 Nov 1650, bur 8 Mar 1651 Delft).  He succeeded his father in 1647 as WILLEM II Stadhouder of Holland, Seeland, Utrecht, Geldern, Overijssel, Gro
2 CONC ningen and Drenthe.  He died of smallpox.  m (Chapel Royal, Whitehall 2 May 1641) MARY HENRIETTA Pss of England and Scotland, daughter of CHARLES I King of England and Scotland & his wife Henriette Marie de France (St James's Pala
2 CONC ce 4 Nov 1631-Whitehall 24 Dec 1660, bur Westminster Abbey).  She was designated “Princess Royal” [1642].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Willem II & his wife had one child: ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * i)          '''WILLEM HENDRIK''' (posthumously, Binnenhof Palace, The Hague 4/14 Nov 1650-Kensington Palace 8/19 Mar 1702, bur Westminster Abbey).  Prins van Oranje Graf von Nassau.  WILLEM III Stadhouder of Holland from birth, 
2 CONC deprived of the title, reinstated 1672.  He landed in England 14 Nov 1688 and acceded to the throne as WILLIAM III King of England and Scotland as joint sovereign with his wife 13 Feb 1689, following the Interregnum after the abdi
2 CONC cation and deposition of James II.  He ruled in his sole name from the death of his wife in 1694.  '''m (St James’s Palace 4 Nov 1677) his first cousin, MARY Pss of England and Scotland, daughter of JAMES Duke of York [later JAMES
2 CONC  II King of England, JAMES VII King of Scotland] & his first wife Anne Hyde (St James's Palace 30 Apr 1662-Kensington Palace 28 Dec 1694, bur Westminster Abbey).  She was proclaimed MARY II Queen of England and Scotland 13 Feb 168
2 CONC 9, following the Interregnum after the abdication and deposition of her father''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''James II.  Willem III & his wife had three children: ''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * (a)       '''stillborn child''' (Breda Apr 1678).
2 CONT * (b)       '''stillborn child''' (Hanserlaersdyck, Holland Sep 1678).
2 CONT * (c)       '''stillborn child''' (The Hague, Feb 1680).
2 CONT
2 CONT * b)         '''LUISE HENRIETTE''' (The Hague 27 Nov 1627-Berlin, Cöln an der Spree 8/18 Jun 1667).  '''m (The Hague 28 Nov/7 Dec 1646) as his first wife, FRIEDRICH WILHELM "der Grosse" Elector of Brandenburg, of GEORG WILHELM Ele
2 CONC ctor of Brandenburg & his wife Elisabeth Charlotte Pfalzgräfin von Simmern (Berlin Schloß, Cölln an der Spree 6/16 Feb 1620-Potsdam Schloß 29 Apr/9 May 1688, bur Berlin Cathedral).'''
2 CONT * c)         '''HENRIETTE AMALIA''' (The Hague 26 Oct 1628-Dec 1628, bur Delft).  
