1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchess_Marie_Elisabeth_of_Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Marie Elisabeth of Saxony (22 November 1610 – 24 October 1684) was a duchess consort of Holstein-Gottorp as the spouse of Duke Frederick III of Holstein-Gottorp. As a widow, she became known as a patron of culture.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a daughter of John George I, Elector of Saxony and his spouse, Princess Magdalene Sibylle of Prussia. She was engaged in 1627 and married in 1630. Her marriage was arranged by the Danish queen dowager Sophie and the dowage
2 CONC r duchess of Saxony, Hedwig of Denmark. In her dowry, she brought paintings by Lucas Cranach the Elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
