1 NAME Dorothea Hedwig /Schleswig-Holstein, Oldenburg/ Gräfin von Rantzau-Hohenfeld
2 GIVN Dorothea Hedwig
2 SURN Schleswig-Holstein, Oldenburg
2 NSFX Gräfin von Rantzau-Hohenfeld
2 _MARNM von Schleswig-Holstein-Sonderburg-Norburg
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 18 APR 1636
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nordborg
3 CTRY Danmark
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 SEP 1692
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hamburg
3 CTRY Deutschland(HRR)
1 TITL Princess
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Äbtissin des Reichsstift Gandersheim von 1665
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1678 Princess Dorothea Hedwig von Holstein-Norburg, at the age of 42, married Count Christof von Rantzau. However she abandoned her husband, and travelled to southern Europe. in 1681 in Rome, she announced to have given birth 
2 CONC to a son, sired by her husband. It is likely that the boy was from an Italian orphanage. After her death, the boy, Alexander Leopold Anton, claimed to be Count von Rantzau, while his 'mother's' estranged husband was still alive. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "He ended up in Holland and the Dutch East Indies. The nobility never fully regarded him as one of theirs, and he and his issue married in a way uncustomary for people of 'his' class in that era."
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Leo van de Pas, Genealogics, [http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00092388&tree=LEO Graf Alexander Leopold Anton von Rantzau]
2 CONT * M. Sjöström, [https://groups.google.com/d/msg/soc.genealogy.medieval/vvwDQ3QKp8I/PTGkXp1N_ksJ Von Rantzau] at soc.genealogy.medieval (Dec. 14, 2012)
2 CONT
