1 NOTE In  English, Christina.  The sole heir of Gustav II Adolph, Christina 
2 CONT succeeded her father at the age of six, a regency under Axel Oxenstierna 
2 CONT ruling until she assumed full royal power in 1644. Throughout her reign, 
2 CONT she attempted to increase the authority of the Crown, and in this she was 
2 CONT supported by the lower estates against the nobility and the Council of the 
2 CONT Realm. The Thirty Years' War, however, had led Sweden into an economic 
2 CONT crisis that Christina was unable to resolve. Highly intelligent, she was 
2 CONT interested in intellectual pursuits and was influenced by the French 
2 CONT philosopher René Descartes, who lived in Stockholm in 1649-50. Christina 
2 CONT never married. In 1654 she abdicated the throne, had her cousin Charles 
2 CONT recognized as her successor, and announced that she had converted to Roman 
2 CONT Catholicism. Self-exiled, she lived the rest of her life in Rome.
