2 CONT
2 CONT 23 December 1744 	Born at the Château de Saint-Cloud and married Leopold de Lorraine, Duke of Lorraine in 1698 and had issue; became the Sovereign Princess of Commercy 1737; she died at Commercy; known as Mademoiselle de Chartres;
2 CONC
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Nature and Appearance
2 CONT
2 CONT She was earthy, even vulgar at times, quoting folksy sayings such as "The snow falls as easily on a cowpat as it does a rose petal." She spoke with a noticeable German accent and disliked dancing, which put her at odds with the Fr
2 CONC ench fashion. Compared to her predecessor, Henrietta Anne Stuart, who was pretty and graceful, Elisabeth Charlotte was stolid and Amazonian. She possessed the stamina to hunt all day, refusing to wear the mask that Frenchwomen wer
2 CONC e accustomed to use to protect their skin while watching their men hunt. Her face developed a ruddy and weather-beaten look.
2 CONT
2 CONT She walked too rapidly for most courtiers to keep up, save the king. She had a "no-nonsense" attitude[clarification needed], and was not given to gallantry, but lacked the prudery to prevent her ladies-in-waiting from flirting wit
2 CONC h courtiers or royalty. Her hearty appetite caused her to gain weight as the years went by, and when describing herself she once commented that she would be as good to eat as a roasted suckling pig.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raised a Protestant, she was not fond of lengthy Latin masses. However she remained virtuous and at times outraged by the open infidelity practiced by the aristocracy. Her views were frequently the opposite of those prevalent at t
2 CONC he French court.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT She is known by different names and styles in different languages with:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Variations of her given names, such as Charlotte Elisabeth, Elisabeth Charlotte and Liselotte von der Pfalz
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Variations of her titles and territorial designations, such as Electoral Princess, Princess Palatine, of the Palatinate, of the Rhine, etc (also in respective forms in French and German)
2 CONT
2 CONT At any rate, the dynastic titles she was entitled to were Countess Palatine of the Rhine and Duchess of Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles and Styles
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 27 May 1652 – 16 November 1671 Her Serene Highness Elizabeth Charlotte, Countess Palatine of Simmern;
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 16 November 1671 – 9 June 1701 Her Royal Highness the Duchess of Orléans;
2 CONT
2 CONT           o Madame was her general style of address and reference;
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 9 June 1701 – 8 December 1722 Her Royal Highness the Dowager Duchess of Orléans.
2 CONT
