2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p11151.htm#i111510 The Peerage]
2 CONT *[http://www.geneall.net/D/per_page.php?id=4450 Geneall]
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_George_IV,_Elector_of_Saxony Wikipedia]
2 CONT *'''Elector of Saxony:''' Reign 12 September 1691 - 27 April 1694
2 CONT >'''Predecessor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Johann-Georg-III-von-Sachsen/299204778280001213 John George III] '''Successor:''' [http://www.geni.com/people/Friedrich-August-I-von-Sachsen-krol-Polski-Konig-von-Polen/6000000001470
2 CONC 080006 Frederick Augustus I]
2 CONT
2 CONT The young Elector was forced to marry by his mother, ostensibly to produce legitimate heirs to the Electorate but truly to end the liaison between John George and his mistress, Magdalene Sibylle "Billa" of Neidschutz. Another cons
2 CONC ideration was an alliance between Brandenburg and Saxony.Immediately after assuming the Electorate, John George lived openly with Billa, and she became the first ever Official Mistress (Favoritin) of an Elector of Saxony. Eleonore
2 CONC  was relegated to the Hofe (the official residence of the Elector) while John George moved into another palace with Billa.
2 CONT Desperate to marry his mistress, John George tried to murder Eleonore, but was prevented by his younger brother, Frederik August. When John George tried to stab Eleonore with a sword, the unarmed Frederick turned the impact away w
2 CONC ith his hand, leaving him with a lifelong handicap.
