1 NOTE She was the daughter of John Frederick, margrave of Brandenburg-Ansbach 
2 CONT (1654-86). In London, Caroline made her home the meeting place of noted 
2 CONT literary figures. She acted as regent on several occasions during absences 
2 CONT of her husband from England and aided the career of the British statesman 
2 CONT Robert Walpole.
1 NOTE "OF BRANDENBURG-ANSPACH"
