1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.deutsche-digitale-bibliothek.de/searchresults?query=%2BHerzog%2Bvon%2BW%C3%BCrttemberg&isThumbnailFiltered=true&viewType=list
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://finnholbek.dk/getperson.php?personID=I14164&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Alexander (24 May 1684 – 12 March 1737) was Duke of Württemberg from 1698 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Stuttgart, he was the eldest son of Friedrich Karl, Duke of Württemberg-Winnental and Eleanore Juliane, Princess of Brandenburg-Ansbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded his father as Duke of Württemberg-Winnental in 1698, and inherited the main Duchy of Württemberg, centered on Stuttgart, from his cousin, Eberhard Ludwig, in 1733.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a successful army-commander in service of the Kaiser, he converted to Catholicism in 1712. He was militarily successful under Prince Eugene of Savoy in the Spanish War of Succession as well as in the war against the Turks. In 1
2 CONC 719 he was appointed imperial governor of Belgrad. As Duke of Württemberg he moved the court back from Ludwigsburg to Stuttgart .
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Soldiered in the Balkans against the Turks for much of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Alexander%2C_Duke_of_Württemberg
2 CONT
2 CONT in German:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Alexander_%28Württemberg%29
2 CONT
2 CONT Latterly (in)famous for hiring and firing "Jew Suss":
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jew_Suss
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Karl Alexander (auch Carl Alexander; * 24. Januar 1684 in Stuttgart; † 12. März 1737 in Ludwigsburg) war von 1733 bis 1737 der elfte Herzog von Württemberg, kaiserlicher sowie Reichsgeneralfeldmarschall.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Alexander_(W%C3%BCrttemberg)
