1 NOTE "OF ANHALT", DAUGHTER OF THE GERMAN PRINCE OF ANHALT-SERBST; LATER
2 CONT "YEKATERINA/CATHERINE II""CATHERINE THE GREAT"; TSARINA/EMPRESS 1762-1796
1 NOTE Catherine the Great of Russia - aka Sophia of Anhalt-Zerbst, or Catherine
2 CONT Alekseevna, Empress Catherine II of Russia was the wife of Peter III of
2 CONT Russia. Became estranged from Peter soon after their marriage. She helped
2 CONT to have him deposed with the aid of Grigori Orlov, Potemkin, Princess
2 CONT Dashkova, and others.  She succeeded him to the throne on 28 June 1762,
2 CONT and the following day had  Peter III imprisoned.  She proclaimed that
2 CONT Russia was in dire danger from foreign domination of her government, the
2 CONT church, and the culture of the country were at stake, and the safety of
2 CONT the nations welfare was in jeopardy.  Her take-over was extraordinary
2 CONT without any bloodshed.  She broke off relations with Frederick II of
2 CONT Prussian, and had her friend, Stanislaus Poniatowski, elected King of
2 CONT Poland.  She won two wars with Turkey; extending Russia's border to the
2 CONT Black Sea.  She imported German farmers from her country to populate and
2 CONT farm this new aquisition - promising them they would be free of army
2 CONT service.  Her coronation at the Kremlin 22 September 1762 was the most
2 CONT spectacular ever recorded in Russia.  During her reign serfdom and misery
2 CONT among peasants increased. But the borders of Russia expanded and increased
2 CONT by her large conquests.  She participated in the partition of Poland
2 CONT (1772-1793-95).
2 CONT She won victoris over the Turks in 1768=1772; and by Treaty of Kuchuk
2 CONT Kainarja (1774) annexed the Crimea.  She thoroughly identified herself
2 CONT with the Russia people - although she herself was German.   She died of
2 CONT natural causes 5 November 1796.
