2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Frederick Michael, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Michael, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken-Birkenfeld (born Ribeauvillé, Alsace, February 27, 1724; died Schwetzingen, August 15, 1767) was a member of the Wittelsbach dynasty. He was the father of Maximilian I Joseph of Bav
2 CONC aria. He was the son of Christian III of Palatinate-Zweibrücken and Caroline of Nassau-Saarbrücken and a member of the House of Palatinate-Zweibrücken-Birkenfeld, a branch of the House of Wittelsbach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Michael was Palatine Fieldmarshal, Governor of Mannheim and finally in 1758 as Fieldmarshal of the Holy Roman Empire commander-in-chief of the Reichsarmee in the Seven Years' War against Frederick the Great.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Maria Franziska of Sulzbach and had 5 children :
2 CONT
2 CONT -1. Karl III August Christian (1746-1795)
2 CONT
2 CONT -2. Klemens August Joseph Friedrich (1749-1750)
2 CONT
2 CONT -3. Maria Amalie Auguste (1752-1828), Married Frederick Augustus I, King of Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT -4. Maria Anna (1753-1824), Married Duke Wilhelm in Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT -6. Maximilian I (1756-1825), King of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had an illegitimate son by his mistress, Louise Cheveau :
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl Friedrich Stephan (1767-1834), Baron of Schönfeld (1813), Count of Otting and Fünfstetten (1817). His daughter Luise married August von Senarclens de Grancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_Michael,_Count_Palatine_of_Zweibr%C3%BCcken
2 CONT
