1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_August,_Prince_of_Waldeck_and_Pyrmont
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl August Friedrich of Waldeck and Pyrmont (September 24, 1704 – August 29, 1763) was Prince of Waldeck and Pyrmont and Commander of the Dutch forces in the War of Austrian Succession.
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal life and military career
2 CONT
2 CONT Karl was the second son of Friedrich Anton Ulrich, Prince of Waldeck and Pyrmont and Countess Palatine Louise of Zweibrücken-Birkenfeld.
2 CONT  In 1728 his father and his elder brother Christian Philip died, and so he became Prince of Waldeck and Pyrmont .
2 CONT
2 CONT The Waldecks had a tradition of military service in the Dutch Army. Prince Georg Friedrich of Waldeck had already led the Dutch army in the War of the Grand Alliance. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the War of Austrian Succession, Karl was appointed as commander of the Dutch Army by the States-General of the Netherlands, as counterbalance to William IV, Prince of Orange, who relied completely on his brother-in-law the Duke
2 CONC  of Cumberland. The Dutch army under Waldeck's command was defeated in the Battle of Fontenoy, the Battle of Rocoux and the Battle of Lauffeld.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1746, Karl became Fieldmarshal of the Holy Roman Empire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT In Zweibrücken, on August 19, 1741, Karl August married his first cousin Christiane Henriette, Countess Palatine of Zweibrücken (1725–1816), daughter of Christian III, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Charles (1742–1756)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Friedrich Karl August, (1743–1812), Prince of Waldeck and Pyrmont
2 CONT
2 CONT  Christian August (1744–1798), a Field Marshal in the Portuguese army
2 CONT
2 CONT  George (1747–1813), Prince of Waldeck and Pyrmont, married Princess Augusta of Schwarzburg-Sondershausen
2 CONT
2 CONT  Caroline (1748–1782), married Peter von Biron, last Duke of Courland and Semigallia
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louise (1751–1816), married Frederick Augustus, Duke of Nassau
2 CONT
2 CONT  Louis (1752–1793), killed in action near Kortrijk
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT
