1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Duke Wilhelm in Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Palatine of Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke in Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	Countess Palatine Maria Anna of Birkenfeld-Zweibrücken
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Elisabeth, Princess of Neûchatel
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Pius August
2 CONT
2 CONT Full name
2 CONT
2 CONT German: Wilhelm
2 CONT
2 CONT House	House of Wittelsbach
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	John, Count Palatine of Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Wildgravine and Rhinegravine Sophie Charlotte of Salm-Dhaun
2 CONT
2 CONT Born	10 November 1752
2 CONT
2 CONT Gelnhausen, Palatinate-Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen
2 CONT
2 CONT Died	8 January 1837 (aged 84)
2 CONT
2 CONT Landshut or Bamberg, Kingdom of Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial	Tegernsee Abbey
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Wilhelm in Bavaria[1][2], full German name: Wilhelm, Herzog in Bayern (born 10 November 1752 in Gelnhausen, Palatinate-Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen[1][2]; died 8 January 1837 in Landshut or Bamberg, Kingdom of Bavaria[1][2]) was Cou
2 CONC nt Palatine of Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen between 1789 and 1799 and first Duke in Bavaria from 16 February 1799 until his death in 1837. From 17 December 1803 to 20 March 1806, Wilhelm was titled Duke of Berg. Wilhelm was a great-grand
2 CONC father of Empress Elisabeth of Austria through his son Duke Pius August in Bavaria.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Duke in Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Death
2 CONT
2 CONT 5 Titles, styles, honours and arms
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.1 Titles and styles
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 References
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm was born on 10 November 1752 in Gelnhausen to John, Count Palatine of Birkenfeld-Gelnhausen and his wife Wildgravine and Rhinegravine Sophie Charlotte of Salm-Dhaun.[2] In 1778, Wilhelm became an honorary member of the Bav
2 CONC arian Academy of Sciences and Humanities.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm married Countess Palatine Maria Anna of Birkenfeld-Zweibrücken, daughter of Frederick Michael, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken and his wife Countess Palatine Maria Franziska of Sulzbach, on 30 January 1780 in Mannheim.[2] Wi
2 CONC lhelm and Maria Anna had two children:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT unnamed son (6 May 1782)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duchess Maria Elisabeth Amalie Franziska in Bavaria (5 May 1784 – 1 June 1849)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke Pius August in Bavaria (1 August 1786 – 3 August 1837)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Duke in Bavaria
2 CONT
2 CONT On 16 February 1799, the head of the House of Wittelsbach Charles Theodore, Elector of Bavaria died. At the time there were two surviving branches of the Wittelsbach family: Zweibrücken (headed by Duke Maximilian Joseph) and Birke
2 CONC nfeld (headed by Count Palatine Wilhelm). Maximilian Joseph inherited Charles Theodor's title of Elector of Bavaria, while Wilhelm was compensated with the title of Duke in Bavaria. The form Duke in Bavaria was selected because in
2 CONC  1506 primogeniture had been established in the House of Wittelsbach resulting in there being only one Duke of Bavaria at any given time.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilhelm was interred at the family burial crypt of the Dukes in Bavaria at Tegernsee Abbey.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Titles, styles, honours and arms
2 CONT
