1 NOTE He was a landgrave, or count, of Hesse-Kassel in 1715, when he married the 
2 CONT sister of King Charles XII. In 1718 she succeeded to the throne, and two 
2 CONT years later she abdicated in favor of Frederick. His royal powers were 
2 CONT sharply limited by a new constitution that granted increased legislative 
2 CONT powers to the Riksdag, or Parliament, and vested executive power in a 
2 CONT committee of aristocrats. The aristocracy was, however, divided into two 
2 CONT factions: the Caps, who sought a conciliatory foreign policy, and the 
2 CONT Hats, who wanted to regain territory lost to Russia during the reign of 
2 CONT Charles. In 1738 the Hats gained a political majority, and from 1741 to 
2 CONT 1743 Sweden was at war with Russia. Sweden lost additional territory in 
2 CONT Finland, and Russian influence reached into Sweden. Frederick was 
2 CONT succeeded by Adolph Frederick of Holstein-Gottorp (1710-71), who was 
2 CONT selected by Empress Elizabeth Petrovna of Russia.
