2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Sophie Charlotte Herzogin von Mecklenburg-Strelitz'''
2 CONT ==
2 CONT  was born on 19 May 1744 at Mirow, Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, GermanyG.3 
2 CONT She was the daughter of Karl Ludwig Friedrich Großherzog von Mecklenburg-Strelitz and Elisabeth Albertine von Sachsen-Hildburghausen. She married George III Hanover, King of Great Britain, son of Frederick Louis Hanover, Prince of
2 CONC  Wales and Auguste Prinzessin von Sachsen-Gotha-Altenburg, on 8 September 1761 at St. James's Palace, Chapel Royal, St. James's, London, EnglandG.3  She died on 17 November 1818 at age 74 at Kew Palace, Kew, London, EnglandG.3 She
2 CONC  was buried on 19 November 1818.3
2 CONT      She gained the title of  Herzogin von Mecklenburg-Strelitz.4 She held the office of Protestant Canoness of Hervorden, Westphalia on 7 March 1760.3 After her marriage, Sophie Charlotte Herzogin von Mecklenburg-Strelitz was sty
2 CONC led as  Queen Consort Charlotte of Great Britain on 21 September 1761.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was sponsor for Sir George William Frederick Brudenell-Bruce, 2nd Marquess of Ailesbury at his baptism at St. George's Church, St. George Street, Hanover Square, London, EnglandG.5
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sophie Charlotte Herzogin von Mecklenburg-Strelitz and George III Hanover, King of Great Britain 1.George IV Hanover, King of the United Kingdom+ b. 12 Aug 1762, d. 26 Jun 1830 2.Frederick Augustus Hanover, 1st Duke of
2 CONC  York b. 16 Aug 1763, d. 5 Jan 1827 3.William IV Hanover, King of the United Kingdom+6 b. 21 Aug 1765, d. 20 Jun 1837 4.Charlotte Augusta Matilda Hanover, Princess Royal of the United Kingdom+ b. 29 Sep 1766, d. 6 Oct 1828 5.Edwar
2 CONC d Augustus Hanover, 1st Duke of Kent+ b. 2 Nov 1767, d. 23 Jan 1820 6.Augusta Sophia Hanover, Princess of the United Kingdom b. 8 Nov 1768, d. 22 Sep 1840 7.Elizabeth Hanover, Princess of the United Kingdom b. 22 May 1770, d. 10 J
2 CONC an 1840 8.Ernst August I König von Hannover+ b. 5 Jun 1771, d. 18 Nov 1851 9.Augustus Frederick Hanover, 1st Duke of Sussex+ b. 27 Jan 1773, d. 22 Apr 1843 10.Adolphus Frederick Hanover, 1st Duke of Cambridge+7 b. 24 Feb 1774, d. 
2 CONC 8 Jul 1850 11.Mary Hanover, Princess of the United Kingdom b. 25 Apr 1776, d. 30 Apr 1857 12.Sophia Matilda Hanover, Princess of the United Kingdom+ b. 3 Nov 1777, d. 27 May 1848 13.Octavius Hanover, Prince of Great Britain and Ir
2 CONC eland b. 23 Feb 1779, d. 3 May 1783 14.Alfred Hanover, Prince of Great Britain and Ireland b. 22 Sep 1780, d. 20 Aug 1782 15.Amelia Hanover, Princess of the United Kingdom+ b. 7 Aug 1783, d. 2 Nov 1810
