1 NAME Mary Elizabeth /Remy/
2 GIVN Mary Elizabeth
2 SURN Remy
2 _MARNM Sanders
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1693
2 PLAC Cople Parish
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1738
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Retrieved from https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Remy-43 and then edited.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Elizabeth Remy was born circa 1693, in Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia, a daughter of William Remy and Catherine Asbury. She died 19 Nov 1737 in Westmoreland County. "Early Colonial Settlers" has her death date as
2 CONC  "after 1738."
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maternal grandmother, for whom she was named, remembered her as "Mary Remy" in her Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT >19 Jun 1709 "Mary Asbury, widow, give unto Mary Remy, her granddaughter, daughter of William and Catherine Remy" [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Will of her father, William Remy, she is remembered as "Mary Sandors:"
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Item I give and bequeath to my son William Remy (spelling) and Jacob Ramy's (spelling) heirs and Asberry Ramay (spelling) and my daughter Mary Sandors and Catherine Wormoth each of them one shilling sterling." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 9, 1709, in Westmoreland county, Mary Elizabeth married William Sandors/ Sanders/ Saunders, born before 1688, in Westmoreland county, a son of Philip Sanders and Elizabeth (probably) Graves. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Elizabeth is named as the wife "Elizabeth" when William Sandors/Sanders/Saunders wrote his Last Will and Testament on 31 March, 1726, in Westmoreland county, Virginia. The Will was probated on 29 June, 1726. William's will me
2 CONC ntions his sons John, Phillip, James and William; wife Elizabeth; daughters Mary and Ursula; daughters Sarah and Elizabeth Saunders/Sanders both not yet 18 years old at the time of William's Will. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Remy and William Sanders, based on his will:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Sanders, II, born circa 1708, in Westmoreland county, Virginia, died February 8, 1768, in Frederick county, Virginia, married Elizabeth Gunnell, a daughter of William Gunnell and Martha Corbin
2 CONT # Philip Sanders, born before 1710, in Westmoreland county, Virginia, died in October, 1769, in Loudoun county, Virginia. Married Elizabeth Hubbard.
2 CONT # James Sanders,  b. 5 Sep 1712, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia d. 17 Apr 1778, Loudoun County, Virginia.   Married Sarah Gunnell.
2 CONT # Ursula Sanders, born circa 1720 in Cople Parish, Westmoreland county, Virginia, died after 1750, in Hamilton Parish, Prince William county, Virginia, married Thomas Walker, IV.
2 CONT # John Sanders, born  Bef 1720, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia nd. Aft 1726, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia  (Age > 8 years)  
2 CONT # Mary Sanders, born b. Bef 1720, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia d aft 1726, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia  (Age > 8 years).  Named "Mary" in Willam Sander's 1726 will. 
2 CONT # Elizabeth Sanders, b. Bef 1720, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia d. Aft 1726, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia  (Age > 8 years).   Named "Elizabeth" in Willam Sander's 1726 will.
2 CONT # Sarah Sanders, b. Bef 1720, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia d. Aft 1726, Cople Parish, Westmoreland County, Virginia.  Named "Sarah" in Willam Sander's 1726 will.  Seen as wife of Robert Coleman but there does not se
2 CONC em to be primary evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT * 1654-1800 Westmoreland County, Virginia Wills [Augusta B. Fothergill];
2 CONT * REMY, WILLIAM, aged 65;
2 CONT * 19 Nov. 1737; 30 May 1738.
2 CONT * Son William; Jacob Remy's heirs; Asbury Remy;
2 CONT * dau.''' Mary Saunders''' 1 shilling; to Katherine Wormoth 1 shilling; sons John, James and Daniel; wife Katherine use of plantation for life, and at her death to son Daniel; Elizabeth Sanders 1 feather bed when she marries.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
