2 TITL Nomini Church by the Nomini River
2 NOTE Cople Episcopal Parish in Westmoreland County, Virginia
3 CONT . . . “Cople Parish’s May 25, 1664, establishment “by order of the court” set the Yeocomico and Nomini rivers as the parish’s borders. Its earliest leader was Sir Nicholas Spencer, secretary of the Virginia colony. He was a native
3 CONC  of Cople in Bedfordshire, England, thus Cople Parish was named. 
3 CONT Yeocomico Church was first built in 1655 of oak timbers and was part of Chicacoan Parish… The Church takes its name from its nearby River. Yeocomico is an Algonquin word meaning “four rooms” and this Potomac tributary has four bra
3 CONC nches. Yeocomico Church was rebuilt in 1706 on the original rectangular footprint with bricks fired in a nearby kiln. The Church became part of Cople Parish upon the parish’s 1664 establishment. 
3 CONT Cople’s other colonial church takes its name from its adjoining river. The first Nomini Church on its current site was built in 1704 and was destroyed by British bombardments in 1814. The present church was built in the 1850s . . 
3 CONC .
3 CONT Cople’s third church, Saint James at Tidwells on the Lower Machodoc Creek, was built as an ecumenical church in the 1890s and was known as Edgewater Church or Boycetown Chapel. It received its current name on April 24, 1924, and b
3 CONC ecame a part of Cople Parish . . .”
3 CONT 2014 Northern Neck of Virginia Historical Magazine, pgs. 7895-96
3 CONT “Westmoreland’s Cople Episcopal Parish Celebrates 350th Anniversary”
3 CONT by Stevenson T. Walker, Past President of the Northern Neck of Virginia Historical Society.
3 CONT Photo – Nomini Church by the Nomini River
3 CONT Event Notice - 
3 CONT NNVHS John Paul Hanbury Award Dedication and Unveiling,
3 CONT Nomini Church, ca. 1852
3 CONT The Northern Neck of Virginia Historical Society welcomes you to join us on Sunday, June 30, as we present the John Paul Hanbury Award to the members of Nomini Church and Cople Episcopal Parish in honor of the outstanding restorat
3 CONC ion. A reception and tour will follow the dedication.
3 CONT For more information, visit - https://www.facebook.com/events/430415264356020/
