2 CONT * Hogg, Bruce; [http://www.freemasonry.london.museum/os/wp-content/resources/frs_freemasons_complete_jan2012.pdf Freemasons and the Royal Society ed 2]; Library and Museum of Freemasonry; January 2012; page 32
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince William, Duke of Cumberland (William Augustus;[1] 26 April 1721[2][N.S.] – 31 October 1765), also known as "Butcher" Cumberland, was a younger son of George II of Great Britain and Caroline of Ansbach. He is generally best 
2 CONC remembered for his role in putting down the Jacobite Rising at the Battle of Culloden in 1746, though he went on to enjoy a successful military career. Following the Convention of Klosterzeven in 1757, he never held active militar
2 CONC y command, and switched his attentions to politics and horse-racing.
2 CONT
