1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Christian William Butler was born in The Hague, the Netherlands, the illegitimate son of Charles Butler and Charlotte Middleton (Myddelton). As a teenager, he went to Aachen near Cologne, Germany, where he studied 
2 CONC textile manufacturing, while changing his name to Christian Wilhelm Mengs. Later he went to England, where he, through the Butler family, got a senior position on the Montagu's estate in Kimbolton. Here he had an affair with Anne 
2 CONC Doddington Montagu, the sister of the Montagu brothers, and they had a son, also named Christian Wilhelm Mengs, who was born around 1734. Not being noble, the Montagu brothers asked him to leave England with their son, and he was 
2 CONC given a nice fee. Where they went first is unknown, but around 1740, he and his son came to Copenhagen, Denmark, where he lived and worked as a textile and wool merchant - trading with European and Baltic countries.
