0 @N6000000002322320398@ NOTE When King John III Sobieski died in 1696, Augustus became one of 18
1 CONT candidates to succeed to the throne of Poland. To further his chances, he
1 CONT converted to Catholicism, alienating his Lutheran Saxon subjects and causing
1 CONT his wife to leave him. Though he regained Poland's former provinces of
1 CONT Podolia and the Ukraine, his reign marked the beginning of Poland's decline
1 CONT as a European power, serving as a protectorate of Russia. When he died, the
1 CONT War of the Polish Succesion broke out. *Deposed in 1704, restored in 1710.
