1 CONT
1 CONT In 1711 Charles had succeeded his brother Jospeh I as Holy Roman Emperor.
1 CONT In 1713 he issued the Pragmatic Sanction to secure the succession of is
1 CONT daughter Maria Theresa in the event that he should die without male heir.
1 CONT Her right to the throne was contested in the War of the Austrian Succession.
0 @N6000000002322348226@ NOTE His reign saw an increase in the wealth and power of the crown and a generous
1 CONT patronage of learning, culture, and the church, even though he inherited war &
1 CONT involvement of the Spanish Succession (1701-1714) from his father. But peace
1 CONT was finally made with France (1713) and Spain (1715), and the country
1 CONT remained at peace for the most part. With the added wealth from the
1 CONT goldfields, lavish sums were spent on the church and the arts. Later,
1 CONT suffering ill health, the government was tended by incompetent churchmen.
