1 CONT Reign: 1740-41
0 @N6000000002322291444@ NOTE Under his reign, Prussia achieved considerable expansion, despite his lack of
1 CONT exceptional military and political gifts. He was intellectually receptive and
1 CONT devoted to the arts, but when he succeeded his uncle Frederick the Great as
1 CONT king, he was unable to perpetuate his uncle's system of personal government.
1 CONT His most notorious domestic measure was his "Religious Edict" of 1788, which
1 CONT gave legal recognition of toleration to a narrow Protestantism. Culturally,
1 CONT painting, architecture, theatre, & music (chamber music) flourished under him.
